-- title:
--   Gluing per-chart addition morphisms over a nine-element cover
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $R$; write $E =$ `projModelCR W.toProjective` for $\operatorname{Proj}$ of the grading on $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,3)\,R$ modulo the ideal generated by the projective Weierstrass polynomial of $W$, and $\mathcal A_i$ for the homogeneous localisation of that graded quotient away from the class of $X_i$, $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,3$. For each pair $(i,j)$ the family `kw_lrSixU W i j`, indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,3 \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,3$, consists of the three chart elements $u_k$ and the three symmetric chart elements of $\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j$ coming from the Lange–Ruppert addition vectors, `kw_lrSixU_locMap W i j l` is the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j$ away from the $l$-th such element into $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j)$, and `kw_lrSixU_toE W i j l` is the corresponding morphism from that affine scheme to $E$ obtained from the chart ring map followed by `Proj.awayι` in degree one. Assume: (i) `KwLRPerChartCompat W`, i.e. for all $i,j$ and all $l,l'$ the two morphisms `kw_lrSixU_toE W i j l` and `kw_lrSixU_toE W i j l'` agree after composing with the two projections of the fibre product of the localisation maps; (ii) every $\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j$ is an integral domain; (iii) for all $i,j$ some $l$ has `kw_lrSixU W i j l` $\neq 0$; (iv) a further family $u_3(i,j,k) \in \mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j$, $k \in \mathrm{Fin}\,3$, with morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisations away from $u_3(i,j,k)$ into $E$; (v) for all $i,j$ the six elements together with the three $u_3(i,j,k)$ span the unit ideal; (vi) each such third morphism agrees with each `kw_lrSixU_toE W i j l` after composing with the projections of the fibre product of the respective localisation maps. Then there is a family of morphisms $\mathrm{pcm}_{ij} \colon \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j) \to E$ such that for all $i,j,l$ the composite of `kw_lrSixU_locMap W i j l` with $\mathrm{pcm}_{ij}$ equals `kw_lrSixU_toE W i j l`; nothing is asserted about the restrictions to the loci of the $u_3(i,j,k)$.
--
--   This is the gluing step in the construction of the addition morphism on the projective Weierstrass model: the Lange–Ruppert addition formulae define the law only on six distinguished affine pieces of $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j)$, which need not cover, and a third auxiliary triple of pieces is added to obtain a cover. It is stated at the explicit ring-level hypotheses actually needed, and is used by [`WeierstrassProjModel.exists_perChart_addMorphism_of_thirdLaw_nineCoverage`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.exists_perChart_addMorphism_of_thirdLaw_nineCoverage), where those hypotheses are produced from smoothness and ellipticity assumptions.
